{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Thread"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Thread\/setThreadSafetyChecksEnabled(_:)"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/thread\/setthreadsafetychecksenabled(_:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"setThreadSafetyChecksEnabled","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"enabled","kind":"internalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default, for every thread, is that they are enabled (as if called with "},{"code":"enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" being ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Those checks are conservative. That means that they will only succeed in considering a call thread-safe (and therefore allow it to happen) if the engine can guarantee such safety.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because of that, there may be cases where the user may want to disable them (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"enabled"},{"type":"text","text":" being "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") to make certain operations allowed again. By doing so, it becomes the user’s responsibility to ensure thread safety (e.g., by using ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Mutex","isActive":true},{"text":") for those objects that are otherwise protected by the engine.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is an advanced usage of the engine. You are advised to use it only if you know what you are doing and there is no safer way.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is useful for scripts running on either arbitrary "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Thread","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" objects or tasks submitted to the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/WorkerThreadPool"},{"type":"text","text":". It doesn’t apply to code running during "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Node","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" group processing, where the checks will be always performed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note"},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Even in the case of having disabled the checks in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/WorkerThreadPool"},{"text":" task, there’s no need to re-enable them at the end. The engine will do so.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"setThreadSafetyChecksEnabled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"setThreadSafetyChecksEnabled(_:)","roleHeading":"Type Method","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot6ThreadC03setC19SafetyChecksEnabledyySbFZ"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets whether the thread safety checks the engine normally performs in methods of certain classes (e.g., "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Node","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") should happen "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"on the current thread"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Thread":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A unit of execution in a process."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/thread","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Thread","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Thread","title":"Thread","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Thread","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/WorkerThreadPool":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A singleton that allocates some "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Thread"},{"text":"s on startup, used to offload tasks to these threads.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WorkerThreadPool","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WorkerThreadPool"}],"role":"symbol","title":"WorkerThreadPool","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/WorkerThreadPool","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/workerthreadpool"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Node":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Node","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Node","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Node","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Node","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Base class for all scene objects."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/node"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Thread/setThreadSafetyChecksEnabled(_:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/thread\/setthreadsafetychecksenabled(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Thread\/setThreadSafetyChecksEnabled(_:)","title":"setThreadSafetyChecksEnabled(_:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"setThreadSafetyChecksEnabled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets whether the thread safety checks the engine normally performs in methods of certain classes (e.g., "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Node"},{"text":") should happen ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"on the current thread"}]},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Mutex":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/mutex","title":"Mutex","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Mutex","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Mutex","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A binary ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Semaphore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for synchronization of multiple "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Thread","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"s."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Mutex"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Semaphore":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/semaphore","title":"Semaphore","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A synchronization mechanism used to control access to a shared resource by ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Thread"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Semaphore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Semaphore"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Semaphore","kind":"identifier"}]}}}